{"name":"Méi Gūi Hóng Red","hex":"#fe023c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Gui Hong","blocks":[{"text":"Gui Hong is a Chinese footballer."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gui_Hong"},{"title":"Prunus mume","blocks":[{"text":"Prunus mume, known by the common name Chinese plum, is a species of tree in the rose family. It is also referenced by its flowers as plum blossom. Despite being referred to as a plum, it is classified in the Armeniaca section of Prunus, making it an apricot."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Prunus_mume.JPG/330px-Prunus_mume.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prunus_mume"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Prunus_mume_fruits_2.jpg/120px-Prunus_mume_fruits_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Prunus_mume_fruits_2.jpg/250px-Prunus_mume_fruits_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thum